{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/504319-knockout-punch-seems-powerful","id":504319,"title":"Knockout Punch - Seems Powerful","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-05T09:51:19-07:00","id":504319,"title":"Knockout Punch - Seems Powerful","content":"So knockout punch... if it hits... knocks people out completely regardless of being Supernatural, Angel, Spirit special templates or powers?<br /> <br /> You can specify how long it lasts AND you can take a killing blow with it with a compromise roll. <br /> <br /> So a few questions. <br /> <br /> Does it indeed work on all Supernatural Beings? <br /> Are there any stipulations? <br /> <br /> Supernatural or fast healing, does it wake you up faster? <br /> <br /> Do you wake up after a killing blow?<br /> <br /> <br /> ....Basically are there any other limitations to Knockout Punch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T10:10:24-07:00","id":504350,"title":"","content":"As ST, you're the arbiter. Your game, your rules.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd rule that it wouldn't work on angels and that other supernaturals get to add their Powerstat (Blood Potency, Wyrd, etc) to their Defence, reducing the demon's dice pool.<br /> Some are probably flat out immune - Sin-Eaters, IIRC, can't be knocked out and I'd personally argue that vampires can't be knocked out either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 05-05-2015, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T10:27:42-07:00","id":504364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilboD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/504319-knockout-punch-seems-powerful#post504319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....Basically are there any other limitations to Knockout Punch?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Demon was written with a lot more ST adjucation in mind than most powersets, so like Eremite already said, the answers really rely on what works for the game. That's the official answer: do what thou wilt. I wish it was a little more clear myself, but this is what we have.<br /> <br /> To better help you, here's what I personally would do:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does it indeed work on all Supernatural Beings? </div> </div> </div>Along the same lines that Eremite said, the way I'd do it is that aside from the occasional minor template mook all supernatural beings get to use their defense against it (remember, in Demon resistance is only a suggestion), major template folks get to add their Supernatural Tolerance to it and it definitely DOESN'T work on some splats, angels first and foremost. From there I'd decide which splats are affected before the game; the developer suggests taking it case by case in each instance depending on the needs of the story but that's a little too fast and loose for me personally.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are there any stipulations? </div> </div> </div>For me, none outside of targeting. If you can get hit with it, you can get hit with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Supernatural or fast healing, does it wake you up faster? </div> </div> </div>I would rule not, since it's not a matter of damage at all but instead is a power based on what the Demon wants. It's like Supress Other Life from Mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you wake up after a killing blow? </div> </div> </div>IF you run it as a by-the-book killing blow thing and you want to give the target a chance to survive, then yeah, sure. In most cases what I would probably do is say, &quot;alright, you put two bullets in his head, roll Compromise at -3&quot; and leave it at that.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's definitely potent. Over the years it's actually become one of my least favorite powers, in fact. But it is what it is, or really what you decide it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T10:49:42-07:00","id":504380,"title":"","content":"Well they're very helpful suggestions and can definitely be used as House Rules.<br /> <br /> Is the intention of the writer/developer for it to have varying effects on Supernatural templates and just was a sort of an oversight error? <br /> <br /> I looked for an Errata or FAQ on the forum but could not find any. Just want a place to point people who like things in writing to abate debating intentions of the RAI versus RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T11:11:19-07:00","id":504392,"title":"","content":"That's what we're trying to tell you: the RAI -is- &quot;whatever the ST wants.&quot; Here, let me give you a link to a related thread so you can see what the developer (blackhatmatt) has said about this and other things, so you can realize how context sensitive Demon is supposed to be.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...es-with-embeds</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 05-05-2015, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T11:38:19-07:00","id":504440,"title":"","content":"To be fair, absolutely any attempt to wake someone up is automatically successful, and talking is reflexive. So if people know how knockout punch works...<br /> <br /> You hit bill.<br /> Someone goes, &quot;WAKE UP!&quot;<br /> Bill is back up to snuff before he even hits the ground. (I'd still make him prone)<br /> <br /> This is pure RAW, mind you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 05-05-2015, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T13:10:30-07:00","id":504533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/504319-knockout-punch-seems-powerful?p=504392#post504392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what we're trying to tell you: the RAI -is- &quot;whatever the ST wants.&quot; Here, let me give you a link to a related thread so you can see what the developer (blackhatmatt) has said about this and other things, so you can realize how context sensitive Demon is supposed to be.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10982-issues-with-embeds\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...es-with-embeds</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wow. I read that entire thread. It's suppose to be very '<i>context sensitive</i>'.<br /> <br /> The kinds of rules adjustments handed over to the Storyteller will not sit well if a game of Demon is played with the way NWoD works. It's fluid, but not so much as say Dungeon World or Apocalypse World or Monster of the Week. The powers do need some more definition, or a side-bar saying 'Storytellers Review this Before You Start Your Game', but even then, they shouldn't have to.<br /> <br /> The other game design follows this from GMC to Vampire and beyond. Powers are usual hard coded and well defined, or their explicitly open and narrative. These seem neither, hard coded and defined but intended to be some-what open and narrative in a system that isn't built for that, and doesn't tell you to build your own or that the powers your reading may need customizing or fixing or game balance for your game.<br /> <br /> I agree with the side of people in that thread that rules should be made for both types, the type who reads it as written and the type who is able to be more fluid, then broken by people who want to break them. Not left broken to be fixed and not without any heads up that this is the intention or the case.<br /> <br /> Roleplaying games that make more work for the Storyteller to tell their stories, make them intentionally inconsistent (which confuses players) without some sort of framework or reasoning, these are not good design philosophies.<br /> <br /> I loved everything about Demon up to this point, but that kind of design philosophy and approach to powers disappoints me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","user":"GilboD","date":". 05-05-2015, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T05:46:33-07:00","id":505289,"title":"","content":"Every game is different with its own quirks, breaking from the &quot;standard nWoD&quot; assumptions. Mummy took the standard dice assumption (success on 8-10) and messed with that, as well as starting at high Potency and falling. Geist started off as a very bare bones, build your own game system with little direction. Beast is going to be crossover heavy, from the looks of it, instead of being self-contained. Every game tries something different - that's a part of the reason why games are so hard to run a crossover with at times. Things do not match up well all the time.<br /> <br /> Demon is heavy ST-arbitration and creation on custom powers (not just Interlocks, but pretty much every gadget) that depend a lot on eyeballing that things make thematic sense together. Demon is a very context-driven, power-customization game. That's a part of the deal with playing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T08:14:38-07:00","id":505554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/504319-knockout-punch-seems-powerful?p=505289#post505289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every game is different with its own quirks, breaking from the &quot;standard nWoD&quot; assumptions. Mummy took the standard dice assumption (success on 8-10) and messed with that, as well as starting at high Potency and falling. Geist started off as a very bare bones, build your own game system with little direction. Beast is going to be crossover heavy, from the looks of it, instead of being self-contained. Every game tries something different - that's a part of the reason why games are so hard to run a crossover with at times. Things do not match up well all the time.<br /> <br /> Demon is heavy ST-arbitration and creation on custom powers (not just Interlocks, but pretty much every gadget) that depend a lot on eyeballing that things make thematic sense together. Demon is a very context-driven, power-customization game. That's a part of the deal with playing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that, and that much was clear in the book about customizing and powers not always needing resistances etc. That seemed very cool to me and I was very on board. Mage is super cool for many of the same reasons. Very free flowing system but with very well thought out guidelines.<br /> <br /> I'm saying the example powers (Embeds) were not thought out (for a few well known examples), and when this was pointed out, it was justified as 'everyone should do their own thing,' then that point was never explicitly stated or pointed out in the book, and what I'm saying here is that's lazy. Knockout Punch easily could have been made the utility power it wanted to be, designers even said and used examples as a utility power, but they didn't, then they never told us (Storytellers) we needed to do it in the book, instead they did so on that thread that I only found by posting on this forum.<br /> <br /> Doesn't seem well thought out, or designed. Hence my disappointment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T16:17:21-07:00","id":506184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilboD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/504319-knockout-punch-seems-powerful?p=505554#post505554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get that, and that much was clear in the book about customizing and powers not always needing resistances etc. That seemed very cool to me and I was very on board. Mage is super cool for many of the same reasons. Very free flowing system but with very well thought out guidelines.<br /> <br /> I'm saying the example powers (Embeds) were not thought out (for a few well known examples), and when this was pointed out, it was justified as 'everyone should do their own thing,' then that point was never explicitly stated or pointed out in the book, and what I'm saying here is that's lazy. Knockout Punch easily could have been made the utility power it wanted to be, designers even said and used examples as a utility power, but they didn't, then they never told us (Storytellers) we needed to do it in the book, instead they did so on that thread that I only found by posting on this forum.<br /> <br /> Doesn't seem well thought out, or designed. Hence my disappointment.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Demon, Matt thinks that the powers give enough information to logically adjudicate their results in context. For example, Knock-Out Punch makes someone behave as if knocked-out without suffering the associated damage. If someone or something cannot be knocked-out, I'd say the power cannot work, because inflicting an impossible state goes beyond the power of an Embed (in my opinion). So no knocking out Vampires with knock-out punch. I agree it is not all 100% clear, but I think there is enough to work with.<br /> <br /> But this context sensitive adjudication is not unique to Demon. In for example Vampire, if a vampire would try to use Majesty or Dominate on a robot, the power would probably not work, as the thing has no mind. This is also an example of adjudication on a case by case basis. In Mage it is even worse, as all creative thaumaturgy must be fully adjudicated by the ST, and could also have different results on different kinds of targets.<br /> <br /> It is true that some systems take more contexts into account than others. Some even have cross-over rules that explain how powers affect other kinds of playable supernatural creatures. But still, it isn't possible to explain effects in every possible context in the book, as in the World of Darkness there could be hundreds of unique creatures that all react in other ways to certain powers, just because their minds or bodies work differently than those of the baseline human or supernatural. So while you call this need for adjudication a flaw, I call it unavoidable. The only difference between lines is to which degree it is necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","user":"Penta","date":".  Spelling 05-06-2015, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}